{"t": 1794114261.295357, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found\n\nCause: upstream ledger release 2026.11 added a `currency` field to every row. reports/export.py wrote CSV with a strict DictWriter limited to [id, amount], so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the API returned 502. Evidence: CloudWatch /ecs/reports-api (eu-west-1), 2026-11-04 19:02:11 \u2014 \"ERROR export failed: ValueError ... 'currency'\" next to \"INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row\".\n\nFix: reports/export.py now exports id, amount, currency and ignores unknown extra fields, so a future schema addition won't take the endpoint down. Reproduced the ValueError before the change and verified the exporter returns CSV with currency after it.\n\nNext: deploy/restart reports-api, then re-test the export endpoint. No other services appear affected."}, "ok": true}
